          "diethyl ether"
        ],
        "temperature": null,
        "time": "stirred 4 h; crystals after 2–3 days",
        "ph": null,
        "vessel_or_method": "aerobic solution reaction followed by diethyl-ether layering",
        "workup_and_crystallization": "deep blue solution layered with diethyl ether; blue crystals of 1",
        "yield": "39.2%"
      },
      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Room-temperature χMT = 55.7 cm3 K mol−1 (0.1 T), close to the uncoupled 2 CuII + 7 GdIII value of 55.9 cm3 K mol−1, indicating weak exchange. χMT is nearly constant to ~50 K, then decreases at low T, suggesting overall dominant antiferromagnetic behavior and/or Zeeman effects. Large magnetocaloric effect: −ΔSm = 34.6 J kg−1 K−1 at T = 2.7 K for μ0ΔH = 9 T; full magnetic entropy content 42.1 J kg−1 K−1 (15.9R; m = 3136.52 g mol−1).",
